# Relative solubility of __MOLECULE__ in binary mixture __MIX_LABEL__ — parameterization __CTD__.
# Same `relative` machinery as the pure screen: no force_qspr, no SLESOL, no DG_fus.
# COSMOtherm's x_RS is on a fixed (solute-referenced) scale, NOT normalized to the best
# solvent, so a mixture's log10(x_RS) is directly comparable to the pure-solvent
# log10(x_RS) values with no rescaling. The solute (compound 1) is held at infinite
# dilution (xs=0); compounds 2 and 3 are the mixture components at mole fractions x1, x2.
ctd=__CTD__ CDIR=__CT_PARAM_PATH__ LDIR=__CT_LICENSE_DIR__ # Global command line
FDIR=__FDIR__ nocompw wtln                                # Global command line (default units — matches pure screen)
!! Relative solubility of __MOLECULE__ in mixture __MIX_LABEL__          # Comment line
f="__MOLECULE__.cosmo" autoc          # Solute (compound 1, infinite dilution)
f="__SOLVENT1___c0.cosmo" autoc       # Mixture component 1 (compound 2)
f="__SOLVENT2___c0.cosmo" autoc       # Mixture component 2 (compound 3)
tc=25.0 solub xs={0.0 __X_SOLVENT1__ __X_SOLVENT2__} relative xsolout_x_log10 wsolout_gg lsolout_moll_log10
